From: mscharged-port
Subject: Compile prepared pipelines in parallel
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

Startup preparation compiled every known pipeline one after another on the
single pipeline worker. Background (preparation) pipelines are now created with
CreateRenderPipelineAsync, so Dawn's worker pool translates and compiles several
at once while the worker builds the next shader modules. Pipelines a draw waits
for keep synchronous creation on the worker, as before. A failed asynchronous
creation is retried synchronously, so errors are reported and counted as before.
Shutdown waits up to 30 s for creations still in flight. The blob cache
callbacks were already serialized by their mutex.

Dawn's default platform pool runs two worker threads. Every Dawn instance now
gets Aurora's platform, whose pool uses all but one processor; Tracy builds keep
their trace hooks on the same platform.

